    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-120030",
      "knowledge_point_id": "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1",
      "knowledge_point": "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios",
      "problem": "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{140}^{∘}\\operatorname{cot}⁡{70}^{∘}}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={70}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {70}^{∘}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{140}^{∘}\\operatorname{cot}⁡{70}^{∘}}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}}}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{cos}^{2}⁡{70}^{∘}}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing  the Pythagorean identity in the form ${cos}^{2}⁡{70}^{∘}=1-{sin}^{2}⁡{70}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{cos}^{2}⁡{70}^{∘}}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}} & =\\frac{2(1-{sin}^{2}⁡{70}^{∘})}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘})(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘})}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘})\\cancel{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘})}}{\\cancel{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}}} \\\\  & =2(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
