    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-26907",
      "knowledge_point_id": "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula",
      "problem": "Find the exact value of ${(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}))}^{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we expand the parenthesis and use the Pythagorean identity.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}))}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡({105}^{∘})+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘})+{cos}^{2}⁡({105}^{∘}) \\\\  & =[{sin}^{2}⁡({105}^{∘})+{cos}^{2}⁡({105}^{∘})]+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}) \\\\  & =1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={105}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {105}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({210}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({180}^{∘}+{30}^{∘}) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘})=1-\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}))}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$",
