    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-327763",
      "knowledge_point_id": "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula",
      "problem": "Find the exact value of $14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}).$\n\n$14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{7\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}) & =7\\cdot (2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})) \\\\  & =7\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
