    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-327247",
      "knowledge_point_id": "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula",
      "problem": "Find the exact value of ${(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}))}^{2}.$\n\n${(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}))}^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we expand the parentheses and use the Pythagorean identity.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}))}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =[{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})]+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=1+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}))}^{2}=1+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$",
