      "problem": "$6\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{10}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{10})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5}).\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5}) & =3\\cdot [2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})]\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5}) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
