      "knowledge_point_id": "143766e0-0ef5-5caf-b699-d394d4a707e9",
      "knowledge_point": "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Products",
      "problem": "Write $2\\sin{15^\\circ} \\cos{15^\\circ}$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=15^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{15}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{15}^{∘} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {15}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
